  "correction_rules": [
    "Model tends to underpredict prices during early phases of upward trends (e.g., after 70.00), especially when sentiment is neutral or slightly positive.",
    "Overestimates prices after sharp spikes (e.g., >72.00) — apply downward correction by 5–10% in subsequent periods.",
    "Underestimates prices when sentiment is consistently low (sentiment < 0.33) — adjust forecast upward by 3–5% to align with mean reversion.",
    "Lagging behavior: model often misses 1–2-day momentum shifts — apply a 1-day lag correction for sentiment-driven price reversals.",
    "When sentiment is high (≥0.50), model overreacts to short-term volatility — dampen forecast by 2–5% to avoid overshoot.",
    "In late-cycle price declines (e.g., below 65.00), model undercorrects — add 1–2% upward bias to prevent premature bottoming."
  ]
}
